      title: "The Workplace Skills Gap",
      titleArabic: "فجوة المهارات في العمل",
      storyTitle: "The Workplace Skills Gap",
      storyTitleArabic: "فجوة المهارات في العمل",
      paragraphs: <String>["A manufacturing firm struggled to fill technical vacancies despite receiving many applications. Its skills audit showed a mismatch between the advertised qualification and the practical tasks workers actually performed.", "The training manager interviewed supervisors and reviewed a competency checklist. Some abilities could be learned through supervised practice, while others required formal instruction before employees worked independently.", "The firm designed a paid training pathway with protected learning time. A mentor pairing supported new recruits, and a skills demonstration replaced an unnecessary certificate requirement for one entry-level role.", "After six months, an evaluation report compared retention and task quality with earlier recruitment rounds. Managers recognized that a reported skills shortage might partly reflect hiring choices and limited training opportunities, not simply a lack of willing applicants."],
      storyWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("manufacturing firm", "شركة تصنيع"), EnglishAdvancedWord("technical vacancies", "وظائف تقنية شاغرة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("skills audit", "تدقيق المهارات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("advertised qualification", "المؤهل المعلن"), EnglishAdvancedWord("practical tasks", "مهام عملية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("training manager", "مدير التدريب"), EnglishAdvancedWord("competency checklist", "قائمة الكفاءات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("supervised practice", "تدريب بإشراف"), EnglishAdvancedWord("paid training pathway", "مسار تدريب مدفوع"), EnglishAdvancedWord("protected learning time", "وقت تعلم مخصص"), EnglishAdvancedWord("mentor pairing", "إقران بمرشد"), EnglishAdvancedWord("skills demonstration", "إظهار المهارات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("certificate requirement", "شرط الشهادة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("evaluation report", "تقرير التقييم")],
      extraWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("skills mismatch", "عدم تطابق المهارات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("workforce training", "تدريب القوى العاملة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("entry-level role", "وظيفة للمبتدئين"), EnglishAdvancedWord("job-based learning", "تعلم أثناء العمل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("competency assessment", "تقييم الكفاءة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("training provision", "توفير التدريب"), EnglishAdvancedWord("recruitment barrier", "عائق التوظيف"), EnglishAdvancedWord("practical competence", "كفاءة عملية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("training investment", "استثمار التدريب"), EnglishAdvancedWord("learning time", "وقت التعلم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("supervisor support", "دعم المشرف"), EnglishAdvancedWord("certificate filter", "فلتر الشهادة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("skills recognition", "اعتراف بالمهارات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("worker progression", "تقدم العامل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("job readiness", "جاهزية العمل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("training access", "وصول التدريب"), EnglishAdvancedWord("recruitment practice", "ممارسة التوظيف"), EnglishAdvancedWord("occupational skill", "مهارة مهنية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("training outcome", "نتيجة التدريب"), EnglishAdvancedWord("skills shortage", "نقص المهارات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("apprenticeship route", "مسار التلمذة المهنية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("workplace learning", "تعلم مكان العمل")],
      grammarTitle: "Passive voice",
      grammarArabic: "نستخدم be مع التصريف الثالث لإبراز الفعل أو المتأثر به. يتغير be حسب الزمن. نذكر الفاعل بعد by فقط عندما تكون معرفته مهمة.",
      grammarExamples: <String>["Practical skills were assessed during a supervised task.", "Learning time is protected each week.", "Unnecessary requirements have been removed."],
      listening: "The new training pathway is intended for applicants who show relevant potential but do not yet meet every technical requirement. Successful participants will receive paid learning time and supervised practical experience. This does not mean that safety-critical tasks can be attempted without training; independent work begins only after the required competence is demonstrated. The evaluation will consider retention, work quality, and the support provided by supervisors. We will also review whether our original job advertisements excluded capable applicants through requirements that were not necessary for the role itself.",
      listeningQuestion: "When may participants work independently?",
      listeningOptions: <String>["After demonstrating the required competence", "Immediately after applying", "Before receiving any supervision"],
      listeningAnswer: 0,
      readingQuestion: "What did the firm change in recruitment?",
      readingOptions: <String>["It stopped checking task quality", "It replaced an unnecessary certificate filter with a practical demonstration", "It removed all training"],
