      title: "A New Housing Regulation",
      titleArabic: "لائحة سكنية جديدة",
      storyTitle: "A New Housing Regulation",
      storyTitleArabic: "لائحة سكنية جديدة",
      paragraphs: <String>["A fictional city proposed a housing regulation for short stays in residential buildings. A policy briefing described the intended purpose: preserving long-term housing while allowing residents to host occasional visitors.", "A landlord association questioned the registration burden, while a tenant group asked whether enforcement capacity would be sufficient. Both sides wanted a clear distinction between occasional hosting and commercial holiday accommodation.", "The consultation draft included a reporting duty and a transition period. A policy officer collected implementation questions rather than presenting the draft as an already enforceable rule.", "After reviewing public submissions, the city clarified the scope definition and published an impact assessment. The class studying the case compared intended benefits with administrative costs, noting that a rule's wording alone could not guarantee its practical result."],
      storyWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("housing regulation", "لائحة سكنية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("policy briefing", "إحاطة بالسياسة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("long-term housing", "سكن طويل المدى"), EnglishAdvancedWord("landlord association", "رابطة الملاك"), EnglishAdvancedWord("registration burden", "عبء التسجيل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("tenant group", "مجموعة مستأجرين"), EnglishAdvancedWord("enforcement capacity", "قدرة الإنفاذ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("occasional hosting", "استضافة عرضية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("consultation draft", "مسودة التشاور"), EnglishAdvancedWord("reporting duty", "واجب الإبلاغ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("transition period", "فترة انتقالية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("implementation questions", "أسئلة التنفيذ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("scope definition", "تعريف النطاق"), EnglishAdvancedWord("impact assessment", "تقييم الأثر")],
      extraWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("regulatory proposal", "مقترح تنظيمي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("housing availability", "توفر السكن"), EnglishAdvancedWord("commercial letting", "تأجير تجاري"), EnglishAdvancedWord("registration requirement", "متطلب التسجيل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("administrative cost", "تكلفة إدارية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("policy consultation", "تشاور السياسة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("enforcement resources", "موارد الإنفاذ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("compliance process", "عملية الامتثال"), EnglishAdvancedWord("draft provision", "بند مسودة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("public submission", "مشاركة عامة مكتوبة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("policy scope", "نطاق السياسة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("housing protection", "حماية السكن"), EnglishAdvancedWord("implementation guidance", "إرشاد التنفيذ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("regulatory distinction", "تمييز تنظيمي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("affected household", "أسرة متأثرة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("consultation response", "رد المشاورة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("policy intention", "نية السياسة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("administrative burden", "عبء إداري"), EnglishAdvancedWord("housing impact", "أثر سكني"), EnglishAdvancedWord("registration scheme", "نظام تسجيل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("implementation capacity", "قدرة التنفيذ"), EnglishAdvancedWord("proposed restriction", "قيد مقترح")],
      grammarTitle: "Reported questions",
      grammarArabic: "في السؤال المنقول نستخدم asked مع if أو whether للأسئلة العامة، أو أداة الاستفهام للأسئلة الأخرى، ثم ترتيب الجملة الخبرية.",
      grammarExamples: <String>["Residents asked whether occasional hosting was included.", "The officer asked which costs worried landlords.", "They asked how the draft would be enforced."],
      listening: "In this fictional policy consultation, the draft distinguishes occasional home hosting from commercial short-stay accommodation. Participants should examine whether that distinction is clear enough to apply consistently. Comments may address the registration process, transition period, or resources needed for enforcement. The draft is being discussed, not presented as an existing legal requirement. In your response, identify one intended benefit and one practical difficulty, then explain what information would help assess the balance. A persuasive contribution should connect the proposed wording to likely implementation rather than assume that either supporters or critics have resolved every uncertainty.",
      listeningQuestion: "What is the status of the policy in this case?",
      listeningOptions: <String>["A rule already proven successful", "A fictional draft under discussion", "An existing legal requirement for the learner"],
      listeningAnswer: 1,
      readingQuestion: "Why did the city clarify the scope?",
      readingOptions: <String>["To avoid all public submissions", "To guarantee results without enforcement", "To distinguish types of hosting more clearly"],
      readingAnswer: 2,
      writingCue: "A fictional city proposed a ____ for short stays in residential buildings.",
      writingAnswer: "housing regulation",
    ),
    EnglishAdvancedLesson(
      level: "B2",
      unitNumber: 2,
      number: 9,
      title: "Media Trust and Doubt",
      titleArabic: "الثقة في الإعلام والشك",
      storyTitle: "Media Trust and Doubt",
      storyTitleArabic: "الثقة في الإعلام والشك",
      paragraphs: <String>["An online article claimed that a local service was about to close. Its anonymous quotation spread rapidly, although the linked document described only a preliminary review of operating hours.", "A newsroom editor asked a reporter to trace the original source. The reporter found a missing context paragraph and contacted the service manager for an on-record response before publishing another account.", "The resulting article separated a confirmed fact from an unresolved question. It included a correction note explaining why the initial claim had overstated the available information.", "Readers debated whether the mistake proved that every outlet was unreliable. The editor encouraged critical trust: checking evidence and correction practices without treating all reporting as equally careless or assuming that uncertainty justified any preferred explanation."],
      storyWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("online article", "مقال إلكتروني"), EnglishAdvancedWord("anonymous quotation", "اقتباس مجهول المصدر"), EnglishAdvancedWord("linked document", "المستند المرتبط"), EnglishAdvancedWord("preliminary review", "مراجعة أولية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("newsroom editor", "محرر غرفة الأخبار"), EnglishAdvancedWord("original source", "المصدر الأصلي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("missing context paragraph", "فقرة سياق مفقودة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("on-record response", "رد قابل للنشر بالاسم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("confirmed fact", "حقيقة مؤكدة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("unresolved question", "سؤال غير محسوم"), EnglishAdvancedWord("correction note", "ملاحظة تصحيح"), EnglishAdvancedWord("initial claim", "ادعاء أولي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("critical trust", "ثقة نقدية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("correction practices", "ممارسات التصحيح")],
      extraWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("news judgment", "تقدير إخباري"), EnglishAdvancedWord("anonymous source", "مصدر مجهول"), EnglishAdvancedWord("source document", "وثيقة المصدر"), EnglishAdvancedWord("context paragraph", "فقرة السياق"), EnglishAdvancedWord("verified statement", "بيان متحقق منه"), EnglishAdvancedWord("editorial correction", "تصحيح تحريري"), EnglishAdvancedWord("reporting standard", "معيار التغطية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("news outlet", "مؤسسة إخبارية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("source reliability", "موثوقية المصدر"), EnglishAdvancedWord("provisional report", "تقرير أولي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("public correction", "تصحيح علني"), EnglishAdvancedWord("evidence trail", "مسار الأدلة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("rumor circulation", "تداول الشائعات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("newsroom uncertainty", "عدم يقين غرفة الأخبار"), EnglishAdvancedWord("media skepticism", "تشكيك إعلامي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("document trail", "مسار الوثائق"), EnglishAdvancedWord("factual distinction", "تمييز واقعي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("news verification", "تحقق الأخبار"), EnglishAdvancedWord("editorial explanation", "تفسير تحريري"), EnglishAdvancedWord("reliable reporting", "تغطية موثوقة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("context omission", "حذف السياق"), EnglishAdvancedWord("source transparency", "شفافية المصدر")],
      grammarTitle: "Reported statements",
      grammarArabic: "في نقل الكلام عن الماضي نستخدم said إن لم نذكر المستمع، وtold مع المستمع. يتغير المضارع غالبًا إلى الماضي، وwill إلى would، مع تعديل الضمائر وفق المتكلم.",
      grammarExamples: <String>["The article claimed the service would close.", "The manager said only opening hours were under review.", "The editor explained that the headline had overstated the evidence."],
      listening: "Before sharing a report about a public service, check whether the headline matches the document it cites. A review of opening hours is not the same as a decision to close a service. Anonymous information can sometimes be valuable, but readers should know what has been independently confirmed and what remains uncertain. In this exercise, compare the original article with its correction and identify exactly which claim changed. Do not conclude that one error makes every source equally unreliable; assess how the outlet gathered evidence, explained the mistake, and corrected the public record.",
      listeningQuestion: "What should learners identify in the correction?",
      listeningOptions: <String>["Which outlet has the loudest headline", "A reason to distrust every source equally", "Exactly which claim changed"],
      listeningAnswer: 2,
      readingQuestion: "What did the linked document actually describe?",
      readingOptions: <String>["A review of operating hours", "An immediate closure decision", "A completed demolition"],
      readingAnswer: 0,
      writingCue: "An ____ claimed that a local service was about to close.",
      writingAnswer: "online article",
    ),
    EnglishAdvancedLesson(
      level: "B2",
      unitNumber: 2,
      number: 10,
      title: "The Cost of Convenience",
      titleArabic: "ثمن الراحة",
      storyTitle: "The Cost of Convenience",
      storyTitleArabic: "ثمن الراحة",
      paragraphs: <String>["A shopping app offered instant delivery for everyday purchases. Its convenience promise appealed to busy customers, but a student project examined the hidden costs behind many small orders.", "Researchers interviewed a delivery rider about unpredictable demand and unpaid waiting. They also compared packaging volume and delivery distance per item, recognizing that larger combined orders could have different impacts.", "The company promoted a subscription discount that encouraged frequent use. Students questioned whether the visible price reflected the full cost to workers, neighborhoods, and the environment, rather than assuming every fast service was automatically harmful.", "Their final report proposed a consolidated order option and clearer delivery information. It distinguished useful convenience from avoidable waste, arguing that better choices required understanding trade-offs that the checkout screen rarely displayed."],
      storyWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("instant delivery", "توصيل فوري"), EnglishAdvancedWord("convenience promise", "وعد الراحة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("hidden costs", "تكاليف خفية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("small orders", "طلبات صغيرة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("delivery rider", "عامل توصيل بدراجة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("unpredictable demand", "طلب غير متوقع"), EnglishAdvancedWord("unpaid waiting", "انتظار بلا أجر"), EnglishAdvancedWord("packaging volume", "حجم التغليف"), EnglishAdvancedWord("delivery distance", "مسافة التوصيل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("combined orders", "طلبات مجمعة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("subscription discount", "خصم اشتراك"), EnglishAdvancedWord("visible price", "السعر الظاهر"), EnglishAdvancedWord("consolidated order", "طلب موحد"), EnglishAdvancedWord("checkout screen", "شاشة الدفع")],
      extraWords: <EnglishAdvancedWord>[EnglishAdvancedWord("convenience economy", "اقتصاد الراحة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("delivery labor", "عمل التوصيل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("packaging waste", "نفايات التغليف"), EnglishAdvancedWord("order frequency", "تكرار الطلب"), EnglishAdvancedWord("delivery incentive", "حافز توصيل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("platform worker", "عامل منصة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("consumer convenience", "راحة المستهلك"), EnglishAdvancedWord("external cost", "تكلفة خارجية"), EnglishAdvancedWord("delivery consolidation", "دمج التوصيل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("subscription incentive", "حافز الاشتراك"), EnglishAdvancedWord("last-mile delivery", "توصيل المرحلة الأخيرة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("worker waiting time", "وقت انتظار العامل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("delivery fee", "رسم التوصيل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("consumption choice", "خيار الاستهلاك"), EnglishAdvancedWord("packaging reduction", "خفض التغليف"), EnglishAdvancedWord("order bundling", "تجميع الطلبات"), EnglishAdvancedWord("service trade-off", "موازنة الخدمة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("demand fluctuation", "تقلب الطلب"), EnglishAdvancedWord("hidden subsidy", "دعم خفي"), EnglishAdvancedWord("full-cost comparison", "مقارنة التكلفة الكاملة"), EnglishAdvancedWord("delivery footprint", "بصمة التوصيل"), EnglishAdvancedWord("purchase convenience", "سهولة الشراء")],
      grammarTitle: "Although, despite and however",
      grammarArabic: "تأتي although قبل جملة كاملة، بينما تأتي despite قبل اسم أو ing. تستخدم however للربط بين جملتين متعارضتين مع ترقيم مناسب.",
      grammarExamples: <String>["Although delivery was cheap, other costs remained.", "Despite the discount, frequent orders created waste.", "The service saved time; however, workers faced uncertainty."],
      listening: "The convenience study will compare individual express orders with a combined delivery placed once a week. Participants should record not only the fee paid but also the number of packages and separate journeys involved. Interviews with riders will explore waiting time and changes in demand, without assuming that every worker has the same experience. The aim is to identify where fast delivery provides meaningful value and where an alternative could reduce avoidable costs. Recommendations should preserve useful access for people who depend on delivery while making the trade-offs more visible to other customers.",
      listeningQuestion: "What must recommendations preserve?",
      listeningOptions: <String>["Useful access for people who depend on delivery", "Every unnecessary separate journey", "Only the lowest visible fee"],
      listeningAnswer: 0,
      readingQuestion: "What option did the students propose?",
      readingOptions: <String>["Ignoring rider experiences", "Combining orders with clearer delivery information", "Banning all deliveries without comparison"],
      readingAnswer: 1,
      writingCue: "A shopping app offered ____ for everyday purchases.",
      writingAnswer: "instant delivery",
    ),
  ];
